Q2.Explore the Power BI Desktop interface and identify the following components: Report View, Data View, Model View, Fields Pane, Visualizations Pane, and Filters Pane. Write a short description (1-2 lines) for each component.
Ans:- 1. Report View
Report View is used to create and design reports. We can add charts, tables, cards, slicers, and other visuals to the report page.

2. Data View
Data View allows us to see the actual data loaded into Power BI in a table format. We can check columns, rows, and data values here.

3. Model View
Model View is used to see and manage relationships between different tables. We can create and edit relationships between tables in this view.

4. Fields Pane
The Fields Pane displays the tables, columns, and measures available in the Power BI report. We can drag these fields into visuals to analyze the data.

5. Visualizations Pane
The Visualizations Pane contains different types of charts and visuals such as bar charts, pie charts, tables, cards, and line charts. It is used to create and format visuals.

6. Filters Pane
The Filters Pane is used to filter the data displayed in a report or visual. Filters can be applied to a specific visual, a report page, or the entire report.

