Q4.List 3 key differences between Excel Dashboards and Power BI Dashboards, focusing on features or workflows you noticed while exploring Power BI Desktop.
Ans:- Excel Dashboard	Power BI Dashboard
Excel dashboards are mainly created using formulas, PivotTables, PivotCharts, and Excel charts.	Power BI provides many built-in interactive visuals and dashboard features.
Data is often imported or copied into Excel worksheets and then analyzed.	Power BI can connect directly to many data sources such as Excel, SQL Server, CSV, and other databases.
Excel dashboards generally require more manual updating and formatting.	Power BI provides easier data refresh, interactive filters, slicers, and cross-filtering between visuals.
